    text: "Njeri lived with her grandfather in a village near Kisii. Every morning before school, she took their goat, Mwezi, to eat grass by the stream.\n\nOne Tuesday, Njeri was late. She tied Mwezi to a tree and ran to school. When she came back in the evening, the rope was on the ground and the goat was gone.\n\nNjeri did not cry. She followed small hoof prints in the soft mud beside the stream. They led through the tall maize to the field of Mama Akinyi. There stood Mwezi, happily eating a cabbage. Njeri thanked Mama Akinyi and promised to tie the rope more tightly the next day.",
