    title: "The Mango Stall",
    kind: "narrative",
    text: `Atieno sold fruit at a roadside stall with her mother. On Saturdays she was as busy as a bee. She weighed mangoes, counted change and called out to every passer-by.

One Saturday, a man bought five mangoes but forgot his change on the table. Atieno saw the coins gleaming in the sun. She picked them up and ran after him down the road.

"You left this behind," she panted. The man smiled and gave her one of the mangoes as a thank-you. Atieno's mother was proud, and she told the story to all her customers.`,
