    title: "Morning at the Market",
    kind: "poem",
    text: 'The sun climbs slowly over the hill.\nThe busy market is never still.\nRed tomatoes glow in shining heaps,\nWhile green kale in the cool shade sleeps.\n"Come buy, come buy!" Mama Joy sings.\nHer voice across the whole market rings.\n"Come buy, come buy, the morning is new.\nThere is plenty here for me and you!"',
